<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bida</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bida is a city in present-day central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nupe-kingdom">Nupe</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>, which formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> in the nineteenth century. It was captured by British forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-lugard">Frederick Lugard</a> in 1901. Its fall was one of the stages of the British conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>'s emirates between 1900 and 1903.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bida.jpg" alt="Bida" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abdulazeez Taufeeq · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Festival_in_bida,_niger_state_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
